Discussion on Tokens and Constants
Five Kinds of Tokens:
Keywords: constexpr, enum, class, long, return. Identifiers: BASE_PAISE, Zone, canTravel. Constants: 1000, 5000, 20.
Operators: +, -, ==, &&. Punctuators: {, }, ;, ,. #define vs const vs constexpr: #define is a preprocessor macro lacking typesafety and scope. const defines run-time constants. constexpr enforces
compile-time evaluation, guaranteeing memory efficiency and zero runtimeoverhead, making it ideal for static fare tables. enum vs enum class: Standard enums leak enumerators into the enclosingscope and allow implicit integer conversions. enum class provides strongscoping (Zone::Inner) and strict type safety. PROGRAM CODE:-
